":\"project specification\"}},\"output_contract\":{\"mode\":\"value\",\"result_type\":\"record\",\"entity_scope\":\"SUPPLY project involving EHA\",\"time_scope\":\"project specification\",\"explanation\":\"none\",\"fields\":[\"funding_program\",\"start_date\",\"duration\"]},\"program_revision\":0,\"rule_binding\":null,\"supported_parents\":{},\"known_observations\":[],\"source_spans\":[[\"s201\",\"d1\",4533,4932,\"These grants are intended to support small, collaborative SWG-led research projects that strengthen scientific exchange, increase member engagement, and build lasting research networks across the EHA community.\\nEvery year, we award grants to projects that will:\\nHelp us build a collaborative network\\nIncrease engagement within SWGs\\nWhat an SWG Grant can cover\\nSWG Grants can cover costs related to:\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s200\",\"d1\",4249,4533,\"SWG Grant-funded projects, 2024\\nSWG Grant-funded projects, 2023\\nHow to apply to join an SWG\\nWebinars and online groups\\nSWG Preceptorship Program\\nSWG Grants\\nThe call for applications is closed. The next call will be open in 2027.\\nWinners will be announced by the end of December 2026.\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s202\",\"d1\",4932,5315,\"Data management\\nData analysis\\nSample collections and storage\\nThey cannot be used to:\\nSupport fellowships\\nPay individual salaries\\nPurchase substantial equipment\\nHow many grants will be avarded per this funding cycle?\\nUp to 5 SWG grants, each up to 30,000 EUR\\nEligibility\\nNon-interventional studies, like retrospective studies or prospective data collection, are eligible for support.\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s203\",\"d1\",5315,5680,\"Applications for basic research projects are also eligible. In these cases, we favor those that:\\nTake advantage of the collaborative nature of the SWG network\\nEncourage the mutual exchange of expertise\\nTo increase diversity and support inclusion within our SWG community, we encourage proposals that involve:\\nJunior members\\nPartners from underrepresented countries\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s204\",\"d1\",5680,6077,\"In all cases, the principal investigator(s) (PIs) must be EHA members and SWG members at the time of application.\\nIndividual applications are not eligible for this call, because each project must foster collaboration and help build a network within the relevant SWG. Please include other SWG members in your project. Non-SWG or non-EHA members will not be counted as collaborators for this grant.\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s205\",\"d1\",6077,6457,\"All applications should therefore be communicated internally within the relevant SWG before submission. Applicants will be asked to confirm this in the application.\\nThe SWG Chair must submit the application, or be copied on the application email. This confirms that the application was presented to the group in advance. Each SWG may submit no more than 3 applications.\\nSelection\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s206\",\"d1\",6457,6852,\"Winning grant applications are selected by the SWG Committee.\\nIn making its decision, the committee considers:\\n• The scientific quality of the project\\n• The importance of the topic for further research/subsequent projects\\n• The explanation of the budget needs\\n• Cooperation and interaction within the SWG or with other SWGs\\n• Other sources of support that are already available for this project\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s207\",\"d1\",6852,7174,\"• The overlap with ongoing/already funded projects\\n• The inclusion of junior members and/or partners from underrepresented countries\\nHow to apply\\nTo apply, complete the application form below and send it to [email protected].\\nThe SWG Chair must submit the application, or they must be copied in on your application email.\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s208\",\"d1\",7174,7546,\"The call for SWG-research initiated grants closed on October 4, 2026 at 23:59 CET. The awardees list will be published on the SWG grants webpage.\\nPrevious projects\\nS